short_label: XII.14
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Cones and cylinders on equal bases are to one another as their heights.
----
proof:

Let {EB} and {FD} be cylinders on equal bases, the circles {AB} and {CD}.

I say that the cylinder {EB} is to the cylinder {FD} as the axis {GH} is to the axis {KL}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="310" height="300" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XII.14 diagram" src="propXII14.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Cylinders EB, FD on equal bases AB, CD. The cylinder CM on the base
    // CD with axis LN equal to GH equals EB (XII.11); FM cut by the plane
    // CD gives CM to FD as LN to KL (XII.13); substitute, and the cones,
    // each a third of its cylinder (XII.10), follow.
    //
    // Joyce's figure draws the cylinders EB and FD with the cones ABG and
    // CDK in them, and the cylinder CM below FD (Ncirc, LN, DM, CC'). All
    // kept; the cylinder CM, N and M are held back until the proof
    // constructs them. Everything added is transparent: faceless twins of
    // the four drawn base circles (AB, cG, CD, cK — the originals have
    // opaque faces, raised over the figure when lit, #140); the cylinders'
    // axial sections EB, FD, CM, FM, standing for the cylinders (lit with
    // their two base circles), with the hidden corners Dk, Cn of FM; and
    // the cones' axial triangles coneABG, coneCDK, faceless twins of ABG,
    // CDK. Draggables (checked against the bundle): G, H, E, L, K, givens.
    // A, B, C, D, F, N, M are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["Gcirc","EAB","Hcirc","ABG","AE","AG","GH","GB","BB'",
                 "Kcirc","FCD","Lcirc","CDK","FC","CK","KL","KD","DD'",
                 "A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","K","L",
