            "AB;circle;radius;H,A,Hplane;0;0;0;0",
            "cG;circle;radius;G,E,Gplane;0;0;0;0",
            "CD;circle;radius;L,C,Gplane;0;0;0;0",
            "cK;circle;radius;K,F,Kplane;0;0;0;0",
            // The cylinders' axial sections and the cones' axial triangles.
            "EB;polygon;parallelogram;E,A,B;0;0;0;0",
            "FD;polygon;parallelogram;F,C,D;0;0;0;0",
            "CM;polygon;parallelogram;C,D,M;0;0;0;0",
            "Dk;point;parallelogram;F,C,D;0;0",
            "Cn;point;parallelogram;C,D,M;0;0",
            "FM;polygon;quadrilateral;F,Cn,M,Dk;0;0;0;0",
            "coneABG;polygon;triangle;A,B,G;0;0;0;0",
            "coneCDK;polygon;triangle;C,D,K;0;0;0;0"
        ],
        slides: [
            { text: "“Cones and cylinders on equal bases are to one another as their heights.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: CYL_EB.concat(CYL_FD).concat(["coneABG","coneCDK","GH","KL"]),
              justifications: [{ ref: "XII.14" }] },
            { text: "Let {EB} and {FD} be cylinders on equal bases, the circles {AB} and {CD}.",
              highlighted: CYL_EB.concat(CYL_FD) },
            { text: "I say that the cylinder {EB} is to the cylinder {FD} as the axis {GH} is to the axis {KL}.",
              highlighted: CYL_EB.concat(CYL_FD).concat(["GH","KL"]) },
            { text: "Produce the axis {KL} to the point {N}, make {LN} equal to the axis {GH},",
              visible: PROD,
              highlighted: ["LN","GH","N"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "LN", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "N", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "LN equal to GH", ref: "I.3" }] },
            { text: "and construct the cylinder {CM} about {LN} as the axis.",
              visible: CYL,
              highlighted: CYL_CM.concat(["LN"]),
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "Ncirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass },
                  { elem: "CC'", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "DM", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "M", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Then, since the cylinders {EB} and {CM} are of the same height,",
              highlighted: CYL_EB.concat(CYL_CM).concat(["GH","LN"]) },
            { text: "therefore they are to one another as their bases.",
              highlighted: CYL_EB.concat(CYL_CM),
              justifications: [{ claim: "same height: as their bases", ref: "XII.11" }] },
            { text: "But the bases equal one another, therefore the cylinders {EB} and {CM} are also equal.",
              highlighted: CYL_EB.concat(CYL_CM) },
            { text: "And, since the cylinder {FM} has been cut by the plane {CD} parallel to its opposite planes,",
              highlighted: CYL_FM.concat(["CD"]) },
            { text: "therefore the cylinder {CM} is to the cylinder {FD} as the axis {LN} is to the axis {KL}.",
              highlighted: CYL_CM.concat(CYL_FD).concat(["LN","KL"]),
              justifications: [{ claim: "cut parallel: as the axes", ref: "XII.13" }] },
            { text: "But the cylinder {CM} equals the cylinder {EB}, and the axis {LN} equals the axis {GH},",
              highlighted: CYL_CM.concat(CYL_EB).concat(["LN","GH"]) },
            { text: "therefore the cylinder {EB} is to the cylinder {FD} as the axis {GH} is to the axis {KL}.",
              highlighted: CYL_EB.concat(CYL_FD).concat(["GH","KL"]) },
            { text: "But the cylinder {EB} is to the cylinder {FD} as the cone {ABG|coneABG} is to the cone {CDK|coneCDK}.",
              highlighted: CYL_EB.concat(CYL_FD).concat(["coneABG","coneCDK"]),
              justifications: [{ claim: "a cone is a third of its cylinder", ref: "XII.10" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the axis {GH} is to the axis {KL} as the cone {ABG|coneABG} is to the cone {CDK|coneCDK}",
              highlighted: CONE_ABG.concat(CONE_CDK).concat(["GH","KL"]) },
            { text: "and as the cylinder {EB} is to the cylinder {FD}.",
              highlighted: CYL_EB.concat(CYL_FD) },
            { text: "Therefore, cones and cylinders on equal bases are to one another as their heights.",
              highlighted: CYL_EB.concat(CYL_FD).concat(["coneABG","coneCDK","GH","KL"]),
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XII.14") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.3":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI3/",
        "XII.10":    "/elements/books/bookXII/propositions/propXII10/",
        "XII.11":    "/elements/books/bookXII/propositions/propXII11/",
        "XII.13":    "/elements/books/bookXII/propositions/propXII13/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Produce the axis {KL} to the point {N}, make {LN} equal to the axis {GH}, and construct the cylinder {CM} about {LN} as the axis. [!just I.3]

Then, since the cylinders {EB} and {CM} are of the same height, therefore they are to one another as their bases. [!just XII.11]

But the bases equal one another, therefore the cylinders {EB} and {CM} are also equal.

And, since the cylinder {FM} has been cut by the plane {CD} parallel to its opposite planes, therefore the cylinder {CM} is to the cylinder {FD} as the axis {LN} is to the axis {KL}. [!just XII.13]

But the cylinder {CM} equals the cylinder {EB}, and the axis {LN} equals the axis {GH}, therefore the cylinder {EB} is to the cylinder {FD} as the axis {GH} is to the axis {KL}.

But the cylinder {EB} is to the cylinder {FD} as the cone {ABG|coneABG} is to the cone {CDK|coneCDK}. Therefore the axis {GH} is to the axis {KL} as the cone {ABG|coneABG} is to the cone {CDK|coneCDK} and as the cylinder {EB} is to the cylinder {FD}. [!just XII.10]

Therefore, *cones and cylinders on equal bases are to one another as their heights.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide: Back in proposition @XII.11, cones and cylinders were shown to be proportional to their bases, and this proposition shows that they are proportional to their heights. The next proposition relates the volume to the base and height in a different way by fixing the volume so that the base and height are reciprocally proportional.
